# Line endings.
#
# This repository is edited on Windows and built on Linux/macOS runners. A shell
# script committed with CRLF fails on the runner with
# "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M", and a JSON file committed with CRLF shows up as
# a whole-file diff every time it is regenerated. Both happened on 2026-11-14
# (altstore/source.json was rewritten with CRLF when it was restored by hand).
#
# Normalise text to LF in the repository; the checkout keeps LF too, so what is
# committed is exactly what CI runs.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.js   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.swift text eol=lf
*.plist text eol=lf
*.entitlements text eol=lf
# A patch with CRLF context does not apply.
*.patch text eol=lf

# Binary: never normalise, never diff as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.ipa  binary
*.cer  binary
*.zip  binary
